The toolchain audit (session spec-isa-audit, 2026-10-28), second part:
forms only the vendor assembler emits (with the firmware's flags) whose
result the printed form leaves no choice in. Masks from the vendor
decoder's table, fields from the vendor assembler; route 42:

- `68 e0 X0 DS` rD.l|h = rS.l|h (X bit 2 the source's high half, bit 3
  the destination's), the other half of rD kept; `68 f0` a pair's head.
- `74 e0 XY DS` rD.l|h = sat8(rS.l|h) (s|u), Y 1 signed: the half as a
  signed number clamped to -128..127 or 0..255, as sat16 clamps a word.
- `9c e1 AY DP` rD = uextra / sextra (Y 1) (rA, p:rP[12:8], l:rP[4:0])
  and `98 e1 A0 DP` rD <= insert(rA, p:rP[12:8], l:rP[4:0]): the field
  from a register, as the immediate forms take it (l 0 the whole word).
- `6e e8` op 1 `[rB+#i] <<<= rS` and `6c|6d e8` op 1 `[rB+#i] <<<= #n`:
  the saturating shift of `__builtin_pi32v2_qasl`, in memory.
- `d8 ed BX SI` (X & 7 = 3) h[rB+rI] = rS.h, X bit 3 the index scaled
  by 2.
- `64 e0` special register moves of retx (2), sr4 (4) and sspn (8), which
  fwtest already holds; and the 4-byte `58 e9 MASK` / `50 e9 MASK` push
  and pop of a list of special registers, when every one is modelled,
  in the 2-byte forms' order.

Not taken, and so still an instruction the emulated CPU cannot decode or
an unsupported one, because the toolchain shows no intent for a detail
the result depends on (HARDWARE-SPEC Q-31 to Q-34): the memory multiply
(-accumulate) forms, the pair shifts with rounding, `><`, `<c>`,
`rev16`, `copex`, the `npc` loads, the pushes with `(c)`, the registers
pc, cnum, uspn, icfgn and icfgs, and the privileged and system
instructions.

The crate tests half_moves_and_sat8, field_extract_and_insert_by_register,
memory_saturating_shift_and_high_half_store and
special_register_moves_pushes_and_pops, and the harness test
registers_halves_and_fields (tests/images/isaregs.S), fail without it.
From the vendor toolchain (PROVENANCE P-1) only.

